.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH taur-registry 1  "taur-registry " 
.SH NAME
taur\-registry \- Manage package registries and operator recipe trust. Not an Arch or AUR endorsement
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaur registry\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage package registries and operator recipe trust. Not an Arch or AUR endorsement
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
Data directory (default: ~/.local/share/taur)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
taur\-registry\-create(1)
Create an enforcing package registry. The existing `local` registry stays exempt
.TP
taur\-registry\-list(1)
List package registries and whether each enforces known\-package checks
.TP
taur\-registry\-add\-key(1)
Add an Ed25519 public key (hex). The private key is not stored
.TP
taur\-registry\-bind\-identity(1)
Attest that a nick and email belong together. This is an operator record, not an AUR check
.TP
taur\-registry\-expect(1)
Record the signed recipe a known package must match
.TP
taur\-registry\-sign(1)
Write a recipe signature to stdout. The secret seed stays in the file you pass
.TP
taur\-registry\-keygen(1)
Create an Ed25519 seed and public key in a directory. Mode 0600 on the seed
.TP
taur\-registry\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Command\-line flags take precedence over environment variables, which take precedence over defaults.
.TP
\fBTAUR_HOME\fR
Data directory (database, git repos, outbox, SSH host key). Default: ~/.local/share/taur.
